// Engine test chapter 1. Exercises text, expressions, stats, flags, conditions,
// choices (with [once] and conditions), calls, and chapter flow. Not part of the story.
@chapter et1
@title Engine Test: Basics
@book engine-test
@version 1
@next et2

# start
## Basics
This is a plain line of text.
Interpolation works: gold is {gold} and hunger is {hunger}.
$ gold = 5
$ gold += 3
$ flag seen_intro
Now gold is {gold}, and the flag reads {seen_intro}.
---
?if gold >= 8 and seen_intro
  Condition passed.
?elif gold >= 5
  Middle branch.
?else
  Condition failed.
?end
$ hunger += 200
Hunger was clamped to {hunger}.
-> doors

# doors
Two doors stand ahead.
* Take the left door
  $ cunning_brutal -= 10
  You went left.
* Take the right door [once]
  $ cunning_brutal += 10
  You went right.
  -> doors
* Open the secret door ?if gold > 100
  This should never appear.
Both paths rejoin here.
~> helper
Back from the helper. Counter is {counter}.
:before_finale
---
-> finale

# helper
$ counter += 1
Inside the helper, counter is {counter}.
<~

# finale
$ roll_result = roll(6)
A seeded roll gave {roll_result}. The doors scene ran {visited("doors")} time(s).
=> next
